            {
              "id": "GHSA-rhfx-m35p-ff5j",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "`IterMut` violates Stacked Borrows by invalidating internal pointer"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Affected versions of this crate contain a soundness issue in the `IterMut` iterator implementation. The `IterMut::next` and `IterMut::next_back` methods temporarily create an exclusive reference to the key when dereferencing the internal node pointer.\n\nThis invalidates the shared pointer held by the internal `HashMap`, violating Stacked Borrows rules."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rhfx-m35p-ff5j",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GHSA-rhfx-m35p-ff5j\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: lru\nFixed Version: 0.16.3\nLink: [GHSA-rhfx-m35p-ff5j](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rhfx-m35p-ff5j)\nAffected versions of this crate contain a soundness issue in the `IterMut` iterator implementation. The `IterMut::next` and `IterMut::next_back` methods temporarily create an exclusive reference to the key when dereferencing the internal node pointer.\n\nThis invalidates the shared pointer held by the internal `HashMap`, violating Stacked Borrows rules.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GHSA-rhfx-m35p-ff5j**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|lru|0.16.3|[GHSA-rhfx-m35p-ff5j](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rhfx-m35p-ff5j)|\n\nAffected versions of this crate contain a soundness issue in the `IterMut` iterator implementation. The `IterMut::next` and `IterMut::next_back` methods temporarily create an exclusive reference to the key when dereferencing the internal node pointer.\n\nThis invalidates the shared pointer held by the internal `HashMap`, violating Stacked Borrows rules."
              },
