            {
              "id": "GHSA-3gxf-9r58-2ghg",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "`openssl` `X509NameBuilder::build` returned object is not thread safe"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "OpenSSL has a `modified` bit that it can set on on `X509_NAME` objects. If this bit is set then the object is not thread-safe even when it appears the code is not modifying the value.\n\nThanks to David Benjamin (Google) for reporting this issue.\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-3gxf-9r58-2ghg",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GHSA-3gxf-9r58-2ghg\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: openssl\nFixed Version: 0.10.48\nLink: [GHSA-3gxf-9r58-2ghg](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-3gxf-9r58-2ghg)\nOpenSSL has a `modified` bit that it can set on on `X509_NAME` objects. If this bit is set then the object is not thread-safe even when it appears the code is not modifying the value.\n\nThanks to David Benjamin (Google) for reporting this issue.\n",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GHSA-3gxf-9r58-2ghg**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|openssl|0.10.48|[GHSA-3gxf-9r58-2ghg](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-3gxf-9r58-2ghg)|\n\nOpenSSL has a `modified` bit that it can set on on `X509_NAME` objects. If this bit is set then the object is not thread-safe even when it appears the code is not modifying the value.\n\nThanks to David Benjamin (Google) for reporting this issue.\n"
              },
