            {
              "id": "GHSA-4fcv-w3qc-ppgg",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "rust-openssl Use-After-Free in `Md::fetch` and `Cipher::fetch`"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When a `Some(...)` value was passed to the `properties` argument of either of these functions, a use-after-free would result.\n\nIn practice this would nearly always result in OpenSSL treating the properties as an empty string (due to `CString::drop`'s behavior).\n\nThe maintainers thank [quitbug](https://github.com/quitbug/) for reporting this vulnerability to us."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-4fcv-w3qc-ppgg",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GHSA-4fcv-w3qc-ppgg\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: openssl\nFixed Version: 0.10.72\nLink: [GHSA-4fcv-w3qc-ppgg](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-4fcv-w3qc-ppgg)\nWhen a `Some(...)` value was passed to the `properties` argument of either of these functions, a use-after-free would result.\n\nIn practice this would nearly always result in OpenSSL treating the properties as an empty string (due to `CString::drop`'s behavior).\n\nThe maintainers thank [quitbug](https://github.com/quitbug/) for reporting this vulnerability to us.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GHSA-4fcv-w3qc-ppgg**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|openssl|0.10.72|[GHSA-4fcv-w3qc-ppgg](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-4fcv-w3qc-ppgg)|\n\nWhen a `Some(...)` value was passed to the `properties` argument of either of these functions, a use-after-free would result.\n\nIn practice this would nearly always result in OpenSSL treating the properties as an empty string (due to `CString::drop`'s behavior).\n\nThe maintainers thank [quitbug](https://github.com/quitbug/) for reporting this vulnerability to us."
              },
              "properties": {
