            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-41677",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "rust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming langua ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "rust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming language.  From 0.9.0 to before 0.10.78, the *_from_pem_callback APIs did not validate the length returned by the user's callback. A password callback that returns a value larger than the buffer it was given can cause some versions of OpenSSL to over-read this buffer. OpenSSL 3.x is not affected by this. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.10.78."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41677",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-41677\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: openssl\nFixed Version: 0.10.78\nLink: [CVE-2026-41677](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41677)\nrust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming language.  From 0.9.0 to before 0.10.78, the *_from_pem_callback APIs did not validate the length returned by the user's callback. A password callback that returns a value larger than the buffer it was given can cause some versions of OpenSSL to over-read this buffer. OpenSSL 3.x is not affected by this. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.10.78.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-41677**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|openssl|0.10.78|[CVE-2026-41677](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-41677)|\n\nrust-openssl provides OpenSSL bindings for the Rust programming language.  From 0.9.0 to before 0.10.78, the *_from_pem_callback APIs did not validate the length returned by the user's callback. A password callback that returns a value larger than the buffer it was given can cause some versions of OpenSSL to over-read this buffer. OpenSSL 3.x is not affected by this. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.10.78."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 1.7,
